  body: |
    # Presence for the stated GB and Northern Ireland arrangements

    ## Authored interpretation

    For the stated cross-border revision, supersession or appeal arrangements, the guidance distinguishes being “in” the other country from casual presence and otherwise retains the original decision country.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    This is the procedural meaning used in DMG 070531–070532, subject to the benefit exclusions in 070533. It is not equated with habitual residence, ordinary residence or international benefit export.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 070531, PDF page 98](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ce3908bed91051df63a90e/dmg0701.pdf#page=98)
    - [DMG 070532, PDF page 98](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ce3908bed91051df63a90e/dmg0701.pdf#page=98)
    - [DMG 070533, PDF page 98](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ce3908bed91051df63a90e/dmg0701.pdf#page=98)

